			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-31T13:01:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				145,
				4
			],
			"Message": "chore(Maintain): Switch Markdown formatter to tabs for stable diffs\n\nRewrite Maintain/Format/Markdown.py to emit tab-indented HTML tables. Convert internal types and helpers to PascalCase (Node, TableParser, FormatTable, Render, AttrsToString), drop the pinned-document SHA guard, extend exclusions to cover .hermes/, Documentation/, Editor/, SideCar/, dist/, and vendor/, and remove `Dependency` from the exclusion set. Update Maintain/Format.sh to register the markdown target, normalize backslash escaping on set/cd, and invoke it by default with no arguments. Advance Documentation/Rust submodule to 62b002eb. Reformat Land/README.md with the new tab-based layout.",
			"SHA": "5c2c48331f21d90352171b7173ab9cade333ad72"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-31T10:02:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				145,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Maintain): Add argparse support and rerun Markdown formatter\n\nImport argparse into Maintain/Format/Markdown.py to accept command-line arguments, then apply the formatter to README.md. The resulting changes remove unnecessary blank lines immediately before closing </table> tags in several embedded Markdown tables, aligning them with the script's intended multi-line layout.",
			"SHA": "5a6163523277833896ac98c06f64541d13cc6969"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-31T09:59:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				145,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Maintain): Add Markdown HTML table formatter and reformat Land README\n\nIntroduce `Maintain/Format/Markdown.py`, a script that rewrites embedded `<table>` blocks in Markdown files into a consistent 2-space-indented layout. It uses a small HTML-tree walker (`_TableTreeBuilder`) to preserve attributes, text content, and tag ordering, while skipping files that contain indirection tokens (`sha`, `commit`, `href=\"./Relative/Path/README.md\"`) and excluding `.git/`, `Dependency/`, `node_modules/`, `Archive/`, `Generated/`, and `Target/`.\n\nApply the formatter to `Land/README.md`, converting the original single-line and tab-indented tables into aligned multi-line markup for stable diffs and cleaner review.",
			"SHA": "bc59b9635565ab22ba09d1ec846b247e06d25bb0"
		}
